Z||000000||lildevil||08-29-2001||07:11 PM||||When i hit the parking light switch it blows its fuse.  I replaced the switch but no luck. Sooooo i am thinking its a wire rubbed through somewhere. But before i go tearing the car apart i was wondering if anyone had some ideas. Could it be a relay?<P>------------------<BR>Earl Sessions<BR>1985 Fiero w/ 1998 Supercharged 3.8 V-6<BR>Best ET: 13.232 @ 101.24 mph<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/water3quarterthumb.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||08-29-2001||08:00 PM||||Check the front parking lights. those take the most abuse of the bunch.||||reg||1
Z||000002||kempo||08-29-2001||10:14 PM||||I am thinking that possibly a wire somewhere is being grounded when it shouldn't.  Don't know much about it, but it's a thought.||||reg||1
Z||000003||kempo||08-29-2001||10:15 PM||||btw- is your car a manual or auto?  wanna sell/trade?||||reg||1
Z||000004||kempo||08-30-2001||10:09 PM||||lildevil- My fiero has just started doing the same exact thing.  The problem is finding where the short is.  I've talked to a few fiero owners, and they said to replace the dimmer switch.  I have yet to try it myself, but I cannot find the short anywhere.  I will let you know when I do.||||reg||1
Z||000005||FaFaFiero||08-30-2001||10:42 PM||||Had the same problem last year. Turned out to be a short in one of the ashtray lights - just disconnected them and all was fine. Hope you find the short - John||||reg||1
Z||000006||kempo||09-01-2001||01:09 AM||||What the problem was for me, after many hours of aggrivation and many a fuses later, it turned out to be my head unit that kept blowing the parking light fuses.  If you have had an aftermarket player installed, try disconnecting it and put a fresh fuse in and give it a try.  Good luck.||||reg||1
